{
	"name": "Reflective Shell",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/light/beam-impact-deflect-teal.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>When you are hit with a spell that has a range other than self or touch, roll [[/r 1d6]] and consult the following table for its effect:</p><table><tbody><tr><td data-colwidth=\"75\"><p>1 - 2</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"351\"><p>You are affected by the spell as normal</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"75\"><p>3 - 4</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"351\"><p>The spell is reflected off of your shell in a random @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-roll-tables.RollTable.XS8Cwgj70GtbcNo1]{direction} determined by the Narrator. Any damage that a creature in the spell’s area of effect would take uses the spellcaster’s statistics and save DC for the purposes of saving throws and damage calculations.</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"75\"><p>5 - 6</p></td><td data-colwidth=\"351\"><p>The spell is reflected back at the caster. Any damage that a creature in the spell’s area of effect would take uses the spellcaster’s statistics and save DC for the purposes of saving throws and damage calculations.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Once you have used this ability, you may not do so again until you complete a short or a long rest.</p>",
